# AmigaDOS boot/script files must keep LF endings.
#
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git rewrote bin/s/startup-sequence
# to CRLF. AmigaDOS then reads the first line as `SYS:SWOS2\r`, which is not a
# command, and the boot dies with:
#
#     : Unknown command
#       failed returncode 10
#
# The release drawer is staged on Linux/WSL so the zips were never affected --
# only a Windows developer checkout running the game under FS-UAE/WinUAE.
# `-text` means "never translate line endings for this path", in either direction.
bin/s/startup-sequence   -text
bin/c/*                  -text
packaging/amiga/**       -text
*.uaem                   -text
